# Validation Rules

Make request validation deterministic.

## Requirements
- Every route must have explicit Zod schemas for params, query, and body as needed.
- Schemas use documented `snake_case` field names.
- Create and update payloads must reject unknown keys unless an owner file allows passthrough metadata.
- Public params and body fields accept `human_friendly_id` (and documented business codes) only; reject internal primary keys unless documented as server-only admin tools.
- Validate `human_friendly_id` format, tenant scope, and existence before service execution.
- Enum values, date ranges, and scope inputs must be validated before service execution.
- Cross-field business rules belong in services only when they need database context.
- Validation failures must return normalized problem-details responses.
- Validation schemas are part of the required test surface.
